Venetium 0066 - 0055's ARM32 codec steering at every resolution: sites send H.264 to the hardware decoder at 144p-480p too.
Asked for 2026-11-01, after a community patch that did this on every platform: 0055 steered only VP9 at level 3.1 and up
(720p+) and AV1 at seq_level_idx 4 and up (480p+), so lower resolutions still decoded VP9/AV1 on the CPU while the
Tegra / Adreno H.264 decoder sat idle. Now, with kVenetiumArm32CodecSteering (on by default, Windows ARM32 only):
isTypeSupported/canPlayType report VP9 and AV1 codec strings that carry a level as unsupported at any level, and
decodingInfo() reports VP9/AV1 of any size as not smooth and not power efficient until real decode stats exist.
Level-less strings ("vp9", "av1", plain WebM) keep working, so VP9/AV1-only content still plays in software.
--disable-features=VenetiumArm32CodecSteering turns it off; x86 is unchanged.

diff --git a/media/base/supported_types.cc b/media/base/supported_types.cc
index 94ec606..9fa4c5d 100644
--- a/media/base/supported_types.cc
+++ b/media/base/supported_types.cc
@@ -265,8 +265,9 @@ bool IsDecoderVp9ProfileSupported(const VideoType& type) {
   if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kVenetiumPreferH264)) {
     return false;
   }
-  // Venetium 0055: VP9 level 3.1 and up is 720p and up (vp09.PP.LL.DD).
-  if (type.level != kNoVideoCodecLevel && type.level >= 31 &&
+  // Venetium 0055/0066: VP9 with a level (vp09.PP.LL.DD), at every resolution, so
+  // sites that also offer H.264 send that to the hardware decoder.
+  if (type.level != kNoVideoCodecLevel &&
       base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kVenetiumArm32CodecSteering)) {
     return false;
   }
@@ -305,8 +306,8 @@ bool IsDecoderAV1Supported(const VideoType& type) {
       base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kVenetiumNoAV1)) {
     return false;
   }
-  // Venetium 0055: AV1 seq_level_idx 4 (level 3.0) and up is 480p and up.
-  if (type.level != kNoVideoCodecLevel && type.level >= 4 &&
+  // Venetium 0055/0066: AV1 with a level (av01.P.LLT.DD), at every resolution.
+  if (type.level != kNoVideoCodecLevel &&
       base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kVenetiumArm32CodecSteering)) {
     return false;
   }
